{
  "esm": "0.8.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "latlon_advection_zonal_periodic",
    "description": "MMS driver: solid-body zonal advection on the global latlon grid, u_t = -omega_deg * D(u, lon) with constant angular velocity omega_deg (deg/s), discretized by grids/latlon/rules/central_D_lon_periodic (2nd-order centered, explicit wrap). Exact solution u(lon, lat, t) = sin((pi/180)(lon - omega_deg t)) * cos((pi/180) lat) — the m=1 zonal wave transported rigidly (constant ANGULAR velocity is latitude-independent, so no metric factor enters the angular-form equation; the cos(lat) profile is carried passively and vanishes at the poles). Periodic in lon with period 360, matching the global recipe closure; no lat operator appears, so no lat BC is exercised here (see latlon_advection_meridional_zero_grad for that). GRID CONTRACT WIRING (grids/latlon/grid.esm): NLAT is closed to 5 at the import edge (the lat axis is passive; 5 pole-to-pole rows at dlat_deg = 45 suffice), NLON stays open (default 144, rebound by the convergence sweep via the loader API); dlon_deg = 360/NLON is an observed whose expression divides by the metaparameter NAME NLON (substituted at load per esm-spec 9.7.6), so the sweep keeps the spacing consistent; lon0_deg = 0. The ic and test references inline the grid's coordinate conventions (lon_i = (i - 1/2) * 360/NLON via the NLON name; lat_j = -90 + (j - 1) * 45 as literals, NLAT being edge-closed) instead of invoking the lon_coord/lat_coord templates: free-name geometry is not resolvable in the bindings' build-time ic/reference evaluator (parameters and observeds are out of scope there — upstream limitation, EarthSciAST tree-walk _eval_cellwise), so geometry in ic/reference positions must fold to constants at load. ERROR MODEL: centered differencing of a single Fourier mode has zero amplitude error and pure phase lag — semi-discrete phase rate omega k sinc(k dlon) vs exact omega k, k = pi/180 per degree — so the relative L2 error at time t is 2 sin(delta/2), delta = omega_deg k t (1 - sinc(2 pi / NLON)): 2.00e-2 at NLON=16, 5.04e-3 at 32, 1.26e-3 at 64, 3.15e-4 at 128, 2.49e-4 at the default 144 (omega_deg = 90, t = 0.5) — an exact O(dlon^2) ladder. The centered + wrap scheme telescopes, so sum(u) is conserved exactly and the zonal mean of the m=1 wave is 0 to rounding at all times.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": ["esd:problem", "grid:latlon", "equation:advection", "mms"],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Williamson, D. L., Drake, J. B., Hack, J. J., Jakob, R., & Swarztrauber, P. N. (1992). A standard test set for numerical approximations to the shallow water equations in spherical geometry. Journal of Computational Physics, 102(1), 211-224. Test case 1 (advection of a field by solid-body rotation), restricted to zonal flow."
      },
      {
        "citation": "Roache, P. J. (2002). Code verification by the method of manufactured solutions. J. Fluids Eng. 124(1), 4-10.",
        "doi": "10.1115/1.1436090"
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "ZonalAdvection": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../grids/latlon/rules/central_D_lon_periodic.esm",
          "bindings": { "NLAT": 5 }
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "u": {
          "type": "state",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": ["lon", "lat"],
          "description": "Advected tracer field over the lon x lat index sets."
        },
        "omega_deg": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "deg/s",
          "default": 90,
          "description": "Constant angular velocity of the solid-body zonal flow (positive eastward)."
        },
        "dlon_deg": {
          "type": "observed",
          "units": "deg",
          "expression": { "op": "/", "args": [360, "NLON"] },
          "description": "Zonal spacing 360/NLON: the grid's dlon_deg free name (consumer-supplied geometry contract, grids/latlon/grid.esm). NLON is the document-scoped metaparameter, substituted as an integer literal at load (esm-spec 9.7.6), so loader-API rebinding for the convergence sweep keeps dlon_deg consistent."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": { "op": "ic", "args": ["u"] },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "sin",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      { "op": "/", "args": [3.141592653589793, 180] },
                      {
                        "op": "aggregate",
                        "output_idx": ["i", "j"],
                        "args": [],
                        "ranges": { "i": { "from": "lon" }, "j": { "from": "lat" } },
                        "expr": {
                          "op": "*",
                          "args": [
                            { "op": "-", "args": ["i", 0.5] },
                            { "op": "/", "args": [360, "NLON"] }
                          ]
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "cos",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      { "op": "/", "args": [3.141592653589793, 180] },
                      {
                        "op": "aggregate",
                        "output_idx": ["i", "j"],
                        "args": [],
                        "ranges": { "i": { "from": "lon" }, "j": { "from": "lat" } },
                        "expr": {
                          "op": "+",
                          "args": [
                            -90,
                            { "op": "*", "args": [{ "op": "-", "args": ["j", 1] }, 45] }
                          ]
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": { "op": "D", "args": ["u"], "wrt": "t" },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              { "op": "-", "args": ["omega_deg"] },
              { "op": "D", "args": ["u"], "wrt": "lon" }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "mms_solid_body_rotation",
          "description": "Exact solution u = sin((pi/180)(lon - omega_deg t)) cos((pi/180) lat) with omega_deg = 90. Derivation: u_t = -omega_deg (pi/180) cos((pi/180)(lon - omega_deg t)) cos((pi/180) lat) = -omega_deg u_lon exactly (u_lon the per-degree derivative the rule discretizes); periodic in lon with period 360; no forcing term. The t=0 assertion pins the ic wiring (reference equals the initial field). The t=0.5 assertion (the wave has moved 45 degrees) bounds the centered-difference phase lag, 2 sin(delta/2) with delta = omega_deg (pi/180) t (1 - sinc(2 pi/NLON)): 2.49e-4 at the default NLON=144 and at worst 2.00e-2 at the sweep's coarsest NLON=16, so the 0.03 bound holds across the whole convergence ladder (exact per-resolution errors pinned in tests/conformance/convergence/latlon_advection_zonal_periodic/golden/errors.json). The mean assertion pins exact conservation of the centered + wrap scheme (sum(u) telescopes) together with the zero zonal mean of the m=1 wave.",
          "time_span": { "start": 0.0, "end": 0.5 },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "u",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": { "abs": 1e-9 },
              "reduce": "L2_error",
              "reference": {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "sin",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "*",
                        "args": [
                          { "op": "/", "args": [3.141592653589793, 180] },
                          {
                            "op": "aggregate",
                            "output_idx": ["i", "j"],
                            "args": [],
                            "ranges": { "i": { "from": "lon" }, "j": { "from": "lat" } },
                            "expr": {
                              "op": "*",
                              "args": [
                                { "op": "-", "args": ["i", 0.5] },
                                { "op": "/", "args": [360, "NLON"] }
                              ]
                            }
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "cos",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "*",
                        "args": [
                          { "op": "/", "args": [3.141592653589793, 180] },
                          {
                            "op": "aggregate",
                            "output_idx": ["i", "j"],
                            "args": [],
                            "ranges": { "i": { "from": "lon" }, "j": { "from": "lat" } },
                            "expr": {
                              "op": "+",
                              "args": [
                                -90,
                                { "op": "*", "args": [{ "op": "-", "args": ["j", 1] }, 45] }
                              ]
                            }
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "u",
              "time": 0.5,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": { "abs": 0.03 },
              "reduce": "L2_error",
              "reference": {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "sin",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "*",
                        "args": [
                          { "op": "/", "args": [3.141592653589793, 180] },
                          {
                            "op": "-",
                            "args": [
                              {
                                "op": "aggregate",
                                "output_idx": ["i", "j"],
                                "args": [],
                                "ranges": { "i": { "from": "lon" }, "j": { "from": "lat" } },
                                "expr": {
                                  "op": "*",
                                  "args": [
                                    { "op": "-", "args": ["i", 0.5] },
                                    { "op": "/", "args": [360, "NLON"] }
                                  ]
                                }
                              },
                              45
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "cos",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "*",
                        "args": [
                          { "op": "/", "args": [3.141592653589793, 180] },
                          {
                            "op": "aggregate",
                            "output_idx": ["i", "j"],
                            "args": [],
                            "ranges": { "i": { "from": "lon" }, "j": { "from": "lat" } },
                            "expr": {
                              "op": "+",
                              "args": [
                                -90,
                                { "op": "*", "args": [{ "op": "-", "args": ["j", 1] }, 45] }
                              ]
                            }
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "u",
              "time": 0.5,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": { "abs": 1e-9 },
              "reduce": "mean"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
